The system llvm22 HIP device backend miscompiles aten/src/ATen/native/hip/Loss.hip
for gfx11xx: a uniform 64-bit scalar-add pseudo (S_ADD_U64_PSEUDO, opcode 4399)
reaches MC emission without being expanded by the SIISelLowering custom inserter,
so the backend aborts with

  fatal error: error in backend: Unsupported instruction : <MCInst 4399 ...>

This is a SelectionDAG-path codegen bug: it reproduces identically at -O3 and -O1
(verified -- lowering just the middle-end optimization level does not move it).
Only this one translation unit trips it; every other ROCm package and every other
torch HIP TU builds cleanly on the same gfx1100/1101/1200/1201 arch set. The
Loss.cu kernels use no wave-reduce intrinsics or 64-bit atomics -- the offending
S_ADD_U64_PSEUDO is ordinary uniform i64 index/pointer arithmetic in the
single-threaded 1d reduce kernels -- so it is a target-backend codegen bug, not a
source bug.

Build just Loss.hip at -O0. For AMDGPU, -O0 switches the device instruction
selector from SelectionDAG to GlobalISel, which lowers the i64 add through a
different path that does not leave the scalar pseudo unexpanded. Source-level
COMPILE_OPTIONS are appended after the -O3 from CMAKE_HIP_FLAGS_RELEASE, so -O0
wins for this file only, leaving every other TU at -O3. Revert once the system
toolchain's AMDGPU SelectionDAG backend expands the pseudo correctly (upstream
llvm has no matching fix as of 22.1.8; the S_ADD_U64_PSEUDO churn there is all
wave-reduce feature work).

--- a/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -934,6 +934,21 @@
   set(__caffe2_hip_srcs_hip ${Caffe2_HIP_SRCS})
   list(FILTER __caffe2_hip_srcs_hip INCLUDE REGEX "\\.(cu|hip)$")
   set_source_files_properties(${__caffe2_hip_srcs_hip} PROPERTIES LANGUAGE HIP)
+
+  # openRuyi: the system llvm22 HIP device backend miscompiles Loss.hip for
+  # gfx11xx -- a uniform 64-bit scalar-add pseudo (S_ADD_U64_PSEUDO) reaches MC
+  # unexpanded ("Unsupported instruction : <MCInst 4399 ...>"). This is a
+  # SelectionDAG codegen bug: it reproduces at -O3 and -O1 alike. Build just this
+  # one TU at -O0, which switches AMDGPU to the GlobalISel instruction selector
+  # and avoids the broken scalar-pseudo path. Source-level COMPILE_OPTIONS are
+  # appended after CMAKE_HIP_FLAGS_RELEASE's -O3 so -O0 wins for this file only;
+  # every other TU stays at -O3. Drop once the system toolchain is fixed.
+  set(__caffe2_loss_hip_workaround ${__caffe2_hip_srcs_hip})
+  list(FILTER __caffe2_loss_hip_workaround INCLUDE REGEX "native/hip/Loss\\.hip$")
+  if(__caffe2_loss_hip_workaround)
+    set_source_files_properties(${__caffe2_loss_hip_workaround}
+        PROPERTIES COMPILE_OPTIONS "-O0")
+  endif()
 endif()
 
 # Compile exposed libraries.
